The Security Council,

Recalling its previous relevant resolutions, including resolutions 825 (1993), 1540 (2004), 1695 (2006), 1718 (2006), 1874 (2009), 1887 (2009), 2087 (2013), 2094 (2013), 2270 (2016), 2276 (2016), 2321 (2016), 2345 (2017), 2356 (2017), 2371 (2017), 2375 (2017), 2397 (2017), and 2627 (2022), as well as the statements of its President,

Condemning in the strongest terms the ballistic missile launches conducted by the Democratic People’s Republic of Korea (DPRK) on 24 March 2022 and 25 May 2022, which involved intercontinental ballistic missiles, as well as the unprecedented series of other ballistic missile launches conducted in 2022, in flagrant violation of Security Council resolutions,

Recalling paragraph 28 of resolution 2397 (2017), in which the Council decided that if the DPRK conducts a further nuclear test or a launch of a ballistic missile system capable of reaching other States or beyond or potentially intended for that purpose, the Security Council will take action to further restrict petroleum exports to the DPRK,

Expressing grave concern that the DPRK continues to develop its nuclear weapons and ballistic missile programmes in direct defiance of the Security Council, diverting vital resources away from the humanitarian needs and welfare of its own people,

Reaffirming that proliferation of nuclear, chemical, and biological weapons, as well as their means of delivery, constitutes a threat to international peace and security,

Emphasizing the importance of maintaining peace and stability on the Korean Peninsula and in Northeast Asia at large, expressing its firm commitment to a peaceful, diplomatic, and political solution to the situation, and reiterating its support for the resumption of dialogue without preconditions,

Acting under Chapter VII of the Charter of the United Nations, and taking measures under its Article 41,

1. Condemns in the strongest terms the multiple ballistic missile launches conducted by the DPRK, including its launches of intercontinental ballistic missiles on 24 March 2022 and 25 May 2022;

2. Reaffirms that the DPRK shall not conduct any further launches using ballistic missile technology, nuclear tests, or any other provocations, and demands that the DPRK immediately abandon all nuclear weapons and existing nuclear programmes in a complete, verifiable and irreversible manner, immediately cease all related activities, and abandon any other existing weapons of mass destruction and ballistic missile programmes;

3. Decides to amend paragraph 5 of resolution 2397 (2017) such that the aggregate amount of refined petroleum products that all Member States may supply, sell, or transfer to the DPRK shall not exceed 375,000 barrels per year;

4. Decides to amend paragraph 4 of resolution 2397 (2017) such that the aggregate amount of crude oil that all Member States may supply, sell, or transfer to the DPRK shall not exceed 3,000,000 barrels (or 390,000 metric tons) per twelve-month period;

5. Decides that all Member States shall prohibit the direct or indirect supply, sale, or transfer to the DPRK, by their nationals or from their territories or using their flag vessels or aircraft, of all mineral fuels, mineral oils and products of their distillation, as well as tobacco and manufactured tobacco substitutes;

6. Expresses deep concern over the DPRK’s illicit cyber activities used to generate revenue for its prohibited weapons of mass destruction and ballistic missile programmes, decides that all Member States shall prevent the provision of any information technology, cyber, or related services that could contribute to these unlawful programmes, and calls upon all Member States to exercise increased vigilance against DPRK state-sponsored malicious cyber activity;

7. Decides that the measures specified in paragraph 8 (d) of resolution 1718 (2006) shall apply also to the individuals and entities listed in the annexes to this resolution, as well as any individuals or entities acting on their behalf or at their direction, or entities owned or controlled by them;

8. Reaffirms that the measures imposed by this resolution and previous resolutions are not intended to have adverse humanitarian consequences for the civilian population of the DPRK, calls upon the DPRK to cooperate with international humanitarian organizations, and directs the Committee established pursuant to resolution 1718 (2006) to streamline and expedite humanitarian exemption requests;

9. Urges all Member States to redouble their efforts to fully and effectively implement all measures imposed by relevant Security Council resolutions, particularly with respect to maritime interdictions, illicit ship-to-ship transfers, and overseas DPRK revenue-generating workers;

10. Reaffirms its commitment to a peaceful, diplomatic, and political solution to the situation, calls for the immediate resumption of dialogue with the DPRK without preconditions, and urges all parties to exercise restraint;

11. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

